2-3. COLOUR ROLES
-----------------
Role             Token          HEX       Purpose
Primary          red-500        #D72638   Main buttons, logo, key actions
Primary Hover    red-700        #A11D2A   Primary button on hover
Accent           accent-500     #FF4D5E   Highlights and links on dark
                                          backgrounds
Background       neutral-50     #F3F3F3   Page background
Surface          white          #FFFFFF   Cards, forms, header, footer
Text             neutral-500    #141414   Headings and body text
Text Secondary   neutral-400    #4F4F4F   Labels, supporting text, form
                                          borders
Border           neutral-100    #DCDCDC   Card and divider lines


4. FIGMA STYLE NAMES
--------------------
color/primary, color/primary-hover, color/accent, color/background,
color/surface, color/text, color/text-secondary, color/border


5. LIGHT THEME EXAMPLE
----------------------
Light theme: #F3F3F3 background, white cards, #141414 text, red
#D72638 buttons.


6. CONTRAST CHECKS (WCAG AA)
----------------------------
Body text       #141414 on #F3F3F3    16.60:1   Pass
Secondary text  #4F4F4F on #FFFFFF     8.19:1   Pass
Primary button  #FFFFFF on #D72638     4.97:1   Pass
Hover button    #FFFFFF on #A11D2A     7.71:1   Pass
Accent on dark  #FF4D5E on #141414     5.68:1   Pass

Corrections:
- #DCDCDC on white is only 1.37:1, which fails the 3:1 needed for form
  fields. Input borders use #4F4F4F (8.19:1) instead. #DCDCDC is kept
  only for decorative card borders.
- White text on #FF4D5E is only 3.24:1, so the accent is not used for
  button text. It is only used on dark backgrounds.


7. PRIMARY BUTTON STATES
------------------------
Default:        #D72638 background, white text
Hover:          #A11D2A background, white text
                (red-600 #C22232 was too close to the default, so the
                hover moved two steps darker to red-700)
Focus-visible:  #D72638 background + 3px #141414 outline with a 2px gap
                (the outline shows focus, not just a colour change)


